  {
    "name": "Hook of Fisher's Delight",
    "type": "equipment",
    "img": "icons/tools/fishing/hook-barbed-steel.webp",
    "system": {
      "description": "<p>A tiny silver fishhook with a gold feather tied to it. Tie it to a line and immerse it in at least a 10-foot cube of water. At the end of each uninterrupted Hour of immersion, roll a d6 - on a 6, a floppy 6-inch magical fish appears on the hook. Roll or choose on the table below. Once it conjures a fish, it can't do so again until the next dawn.</p><table><tr><th>d8</th><th>Fish</th><th>Effect</th></tr><tr><td>1-4</td><td>Green, copper bands</td><td>A day's nourishment for one creature if eaten within 24 Hours, then it rots.</td></tr><tr><td>5-6</td><td>Yellow, black stripes</td><td>Thrown up to Far at a Being it can see: pass [Reflex] or be knocked Prone. The fish then vanishes.</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Blue, white bands</td><td>Sprouts wings and sings sweetly, following you around for 2d4 Hours or until it drops to 0 HP (HD: 1, 4 HP, Fly 30').</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Gold, silver stripes</td><td>A day's nourishment and 2d10 temporary HP if eaten within 24 Hours, then it rots.</td></tr></table>",
